  "next_intervention": {
    "pick": "Trace and rebalance THREE_POINT shot resolution (shot_resolution.py: shot_make_probability and its upstream contest_bucket/release_mode assignment) so that a shooter's own real skill separation survives into simulated team shooting-percentage output.",
    "second_priority_not_this_phase": "Wiring the already-computed but disabled foul_drawing_shrunk_rate into the free-throw dispatch path (a small, low-risk, already-scoped fix per possession_orchestrator.py's own documented TODO) -- deprioritized behind the 3PT/2PT fix above only because FT rate is a smaller share of total scoring, not because it is unimportant.",
    "superseded_note": "SUPERSEDED by three-point resolution diagnostic (backtests/three_point_resolution_before.json): the ~98%-erased 3PT figure compared single-game realized box-score gaps (noise-dominated) with a simulated gap aggregated over team sets that overlapped (a team can be both strong and weak across games). Per-game paired, the sim gap (0.36pp) tracks its expected make-probability gap (0.54pp); shot_make_probability passes skill through at slope ~0.98.",
    "why_this_one_first": "Of every measured collapse point, this is the single largest (three_pt_pct gap erased ~98%, from a real 5.3-percentage-point strong/weak gap down to 0.09 simulated) and it sits directly on the primary scoring pathway (2PT/3PT efficiency dominates total points, unlike FT rate). The engine INPUTS feeding it are already real and correctly directioned (rank 1 finding here is downstream of a working input pipeline, not a broken one) -- so fixing this one link has the largest plausible effect on closing the large/extreme margin-compression gap, without reopening rebounding, defense, turnovers, pace, or calibration."
  },
